    <div class="tg-hero__inner">
      <span class="tg-hero__type">Topical Study · Six Parts</span>
      <h1 class="tg-hero__title">The Papacy</h1>
      <p class="tg-hero__intro">
        Is the papacy an office Christ instituted, or a development that grew past
        — and at points against — what Scripture teaches about authority in the
        church? The question is usually argued as one thing. It is at least seven
        things, and they are not equally supported. This study separates them,
        examines every text that bears on them, quotes the historical record from
        the primary sources rather than from summaries of them, states each side's
        best case in the form its own best advocates would recognise, and then says
        plainly where the ground is firm.
      </p>
      <blockquote class="tg-hero__key-verse">
        <p>And I tell you that you are Peter, and on this rock I will build My church,
           and the gates of Hades will not prevail against it.</p>
        <cite><a class="ref" data-ref="Matthew 16:18">Matthew 16:18</a></cite>
      </blockquote>
    </div>
  </header><main style="--tg-accent: #6b2137">
